---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SERVER } from '../consts.ts';
---
<Base title="FAQ — GibbSux">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">QUESTIONS</span>
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <p class="lead">If your question isn't here, ask on Discord.</p>
    </div>

    <details open>
      <summary>How do I get whitelisted?</summary>
      <p>Send your exact Minecraft username on <a href={SERVER.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord</a>.
      Names are case-sensitive, so copy it from your launcher rather than typing it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I play on Bedrock, console or my phone?</summary>
      <p>No. This is Java Edition only. Bedrock uses a completely different network
      protocol and cannot connect.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a paid Minecraft account?</summary>
      <p>Yes. The server verifies every login with Mojang, so cracked clients are
      rejected. This is also what stops people impersonating you.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is the server on 24/7?</summary>
      <p>Mostly. It runs on a Raspberry Pi at home, so it goes down occasionally for
      updates, power cuts or internet problems. Check the live status on the home page.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will my builds get deleted?</summary>
      <p>No. There are no scheduled resets, and the world is backed up every night to
      off-site storage. If something goes badly wrong we can roll back.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why can I see so far?</summary>
      <p>The server pregenerates terrain and stores Distant Horizons LOD data for it, then sends
      that to you when you join. You see the whole pregenerated area without having explored it.
      You need Distant Horizons <b>3.2.0-b</b> client-side — the <a href="/mods#modpack">modpack</a> has it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>I installed Distant Horizons but see nothing at distance</summary>
      <p>Almost always a version mismatch. The server runs 3.2.0-b and only talks to clients on the
      same build. A different version fails silently — no error, just no terrain. Use the
      <a href="/mods#modpack">modpack</a> to be sure.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I have to use the modpack?</summary>
      <p>No. Vanilla Fabric works, and any client-side mods are fine. The pack is just the fast path,
      and it guarantees the right Distant Horizons version.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I use shaders?</summary>
      <p>Yes — Iris plus Sodium. Shaders are entirely client-side, so it's purely a
      question of what your GPU can handle.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why do I get kicked as soon as I join?</summary>
      <p>You have a mod installed that adds content the server doesn't have. Make a clean
      Fabric instance with only client-side mods. See the <a href="/mods">Mods page</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why is my ping high?</summary>
      <p>The server is reached through a free tunnel that routes players based on their
      ISP, and it occasionally picks a distant datacenter. Usually it's fine within Europe.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I invite a friend?</summary>
      <p>Ask first. It's a small server and everyone here was vouched for by someone.
      Usually the answer is yes.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can we add a modpack?</summary>
      <p>Possible, but it means every player installs the same pack at the same versions,
      and probably a fresh world. If several people want it, bring it up on Discord.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What hardware does it run on?</summary>
      <p>A Raspberry Pi 5 with 16GB of RAM, running Fabric with performance mods
      (Lithium, C2ME, FerriteCore, Krypton). Startup takes about five seconds.</p>
    </details>
  </section>
</Base>
